//
// PROBE: `bund.eval`, `bund.eval.` and `!!` — evaluate a string of Bund code
// in this VM, on its stacks and against its word table.
//
// The string is parsed and each value applied in turn, exactly as a program's
// own values are (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/helpers/eval.rs:7-45). So the code
// sees the stack it was called on, and a word it registers stays registered.
// `bund.eval.` takes the string from the workbench, and `!!` aliases
// `bund.eval` (reference/Bund/src/stdlib/functions/create_aliases.rs:13).
// Only succeeding cases: a failure inside the string is reported with a
// wrapper Bund2 does not print (D36).
//
"probe: bund.eval runs code on the stack it was called on" println
"1 2 +" bund.eval println
10 "5 +" bund.eval println
"probe: a word registered inside the string stays registered" println
":sq { dup * } register" bund.eval
7 sq println
"probe: bund.eval. takes the string from the workbench" println
"3 4 *" . bund.eval. println
"probe: !! is bund.eval" println
"6 7 +" !! println
